152	
153	Table~\ref{tab:scs-validation} shows that SCS from both embeddings significantly predicts empirical confusion.
154	The correlation is moderate ($\rho{=}0.14$--$0.31$), indicating that SCS is a valid but partial proxy: confusability has dimensions beyond embedding similarity (e.g., context-dependent ambiguity, frequency-driven familiarity).
155	This ``valid but partial'' status supports using SCS for correlational analysis while explaining why SCS-based decomposition (SDGD-zero) underperforms empirical-confusion-based decomposition (SDGD-cal).
156	
157	\subsection{DocRED Confusability Study}
158	\label{sec:docred}
159	
160	We extend the confusability analysis to DocRED (96 document-level relation types), providing a third RE dataset for cross-task validation.
